{"code":"ko","name":"Korean","native":"한국어","phase":1,"medium":"en","file_level":"B1","level":{"title":"Intermediate: long negation, ability, honorifics, opinions","goals":["Negate formally and express ability","Talk family with honorifics","Argue opinions and describe weather"],"units":[{"id":"B1-U1","title":"Negation and ability","lessons":[{"id":"B1-U1-L1","title":"-지 않다 / -지 못하다","learn":"Formal negation! 먹지 않아요 (I don't eat — formal), 가지 않아요. CAN'T: 먹지 못해요 (I can't eat / unable). 안 = casual, -지 않다 = formal writing and speeches. Reason: 왜냐하면…그래서!","vocab":[{"t":"먹지 않아요","r":"meokji an-ayo","en":"don't eat (formal)","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"가지 않아요","r":"gaji an-ayo","en":"don't go (formal)","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"하지 않아요","r":"haji an-ayo","en":"don't do (formal)","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"먹지 못해요","r":"meokji motaeyo","en":"can't eat","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"가지 못해요","r":"gaji motaeyo","en":"can't go","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"몰라요","r":"mollayo","en":"don't know","pos":"verb"},{"t":"왜냐하면","r":"waenyahamyeon","en":"because","pos":"conjunction"},{"t":"그래서","r":"geuraeseo","en":"so / therefore","pos":"conjunction"}],"grammar":{"title":"-지 않다 (won't) · -지 못하다 (can't)","explain":"안 먹어요 = don't eat (casual), 먹지 않아요 = don't eat (formal). 먹지 못해요 = CAN'T eat (unable). 못 = unable, 안 = unwilling!","pattern":"-지 않다 · -지 못하다","examples":[{"t":"오늘은 먹지 않아요.","r":"oneul-eun meokji an-ayo.","en":"Today I don't eat. (formal)"},{"t":"갈 수 없어요. 가지 못해요.","r":"gal su eops-eoyo. gaji motaeyo.","en":"I can't go. I'm unable to go."},{"t":"왜냐하면 아파요. 그래서 쉬어요.","r":"waenyahamyeon apayo. geuraeseo swieoyo.","en":"Because I'm sick. So I rest."}],"mistakes":["Using -지 않다 with friends — friends: 안!","Saying 안 못 가요 — pick ONE: 못 가요!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"미나","t":"같이 먹지 않을래요?","r":"gachi meokji an-eullaeyo?","en":"Won't you eat together?"},{"sp":"지훈","t":"미안해요, 아파서 못 먹어요.","r":"mianhaeyo, apaseo mot meog-eoyo.","en":"Sorry, I'm sick so I can't eat."},{"sp":"미나","t":"알겠어요! 잘 쉬어요!","r":"algess-eoyo! jal swieoyo!","en":"Got it! Rest well!"},{"sp":"지훈","t":"고마워요!","r":"gomawoyo!","en":"Thanks!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say (formal): I don't eat today","answer":"오늘은 먹지 않아요"},{"type":"fill","q":"가지 ___. (can't go)","answer":"못해요"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Because I'm sick. So I rest' is…","options":["아파서 쉬어요","왜냐하면 아파요. 그래서 쉬어요","아프니까 쉴 거예요","아파도 쉬어요"],"answer":"왜냐하면 아파요. 그래서 쉬어요"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: 않아요 / 먹지 / 오늘은","answer":"오늘은 먹지 않아요"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: 오늘은 먹지 않아요.","answer":"오늘은 먹지 않아요."}],"quiz":[{"q":"-지 않다 is…","options":["casual negative","formal negative","past","command"],"answer":1,"why":"먹지 않아요 — formal."},{"q":"먹지 못해요 means…","options":["won't eat","can't eat","didn't eat","don't eat"],"answer":1,"why":"못 = unable."},{"q":"왜냐하면…그래서 links…","options":["two nouns","reason → result","questions","commands"],"answer":1,"why":"Because…so…"},{"q":"몰라요 means…","options":["I know","I don't know","I forgot","I remember"],"answer":1,"why":"몰라요 = don't know."},{"q":"안 vs 못: the difference is…","options":["past/future","unwilling/unable","loud/quiet","fast/slow"],"answer":1,"why":"안 = won't, 못 = can't."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Formal negation worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Korean.","items":["don't eat (formal)","can't go","because"],"key":["먹지 않아요","가지 못해요","왜냐하면"]},{"instruction":"Formal vs can't.","items":["Today I don't eat (formal)","I can't go","Because I'm sick. So I rest"],"key":["오늘은 먹지 않아요","가지 못해요","왜냐하면 아파요. 그래서 쉬어요"]},{"instruction":"Invite.","items":["Won't you eat together?","Rest well!"],"key":["같이 먹지 않을래요","잘 쉬어요"]}]}},{"id":"B1-U1-L2","title":"Can and plan: -(으)ㄹ 수 / -(으)려고","learn":"Ability! -(으)ㄹ 수 있어요 (can): 할 수 있어요, 먹을 수 있어요. Can't: 수 없어요. Plans: -(으)려고 해요 (I plan to): 가려고 해요! Ability + plans = B1 power!","vocab":[{"t":"할 수 있어요","r":"hal su iss-eoyo","en":"can do","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"먹을 수 있어요","r":"meog-eul su iss-eoyo","en":"can eat","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"갈 수 있어요","r":"gal su iss-eoyo","en":"can go","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"볼 수 있어요","r":"bol su iss-eoyo","en":"can see","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"하려고 해요","r":"haryeogo haeyo","en":"plan to do","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"가려고 해요","r":"garyeogo haeyo","en":"plan to go","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"먹으려고 해요","r":"meog-euryeogo haeyo","en":"plan to eat","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"배우려고 해요","r":"bae-uryeogo haeyo","en":"plan to learn","pos":"phrase"}],"grammar":{"title":"-(으)ㄹ 수 있어요 · -(으)려고","explain":"할 수 있어요 (can do), 할 수 없어요 (can't). Vowel-stems: 갈 수, consonant: 먹을 수! Plans: 한국에 가려고 해요 (I plan to go to Korea)!","pattern":"(으)ㄹ 수 있어요/없어요 · (으)려고 해요","examples":[{"t":"한국어를 할 수 있어요.","r":"hangug-eo-reul hal su iss-eoyo.","en":"I can speak Korean."},{"t":"김치를 먹을 수 있어요.","r":"gimchi-reul meog-eul su iss-eoyo.","en":"I can eat kimchi."},{"t":"한국에 가려고 해요!","r":"hangug-e garyeogo haeyo!","en":"I plan to go to Korea!"}],"mistakes":["Saying 할 수 있다 politely — polite: 수 있어요!","Saying 가려고요 — plans: -(으)려고 해요!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"지훈","t":"한국어를 할 수 있어요?","r":"hangug-eo-reul hal su iss-eoyo?","en":"Can you speak Korean?"},{"sp":"미나","t":"네, 조금 할 수 있어요!","r":"ne, jogeum hal su iss-eoyo!","en":"Yes, I can a little!"},{"sp":"지훈","t":"대단해요! 뭐 하려고 해요?","r":"daedanhaeyo! mwo haryeogo haeyo?","en":"Amazing! What do you plan to do?"},{"sp":"미나","t":"김치를 먹으려고 해요!","r":"gimchi-reul meog-euryeogo haeyo!","en":"I plan to eat kimchi!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I can speak Korean","answer":"한국어를 할 수 있어요"},{"type":"fill","q":"한국에 가___ 해요. (plan to)","answer":"려고"},{"type":"choose","q":"'I plan to eat kimchi' is…","options":["김치를 먹고 싶어요","김치를 먹으려고 해요","김치를 먹을 수 있어요","김치를 먹었어요"],"answer":"김치를 먹으려고 해요"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: 있어요 / 수 / 할","answer":"할 수 있어요"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: 한국어를 할 수 있어요.","answer":"한국어를 할 수 있어요."}],"quiz":[{"q":"할 수 있어요 means…","options":["do (habit)","can do","want do","did"],"answer":1,"why":"수 있어요 = can."},{"q":"할 수 없어요 means…","options":["don't do","can't do","didn't do","won't do"],"answer":1,"why":"수 없어요 = can't."},{"q":"가려고 해요 means…","options":["I go","I plan to go","I can go","I went"],"answer":1,"why":"-(으)려고 = plan to."},{"q":"Consonant-stems take…","options":["-ㄹ 수","-을 수","-를 수","-를수"],"answer":1,"why":"먹을 수 — 을 after consonants."},{"q":"조금 means…","options":["a lot","a little","never","always"],"answer":1,"why":"조금 = a little."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Ability worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Korean.","items":["can do","plan to go","a little"],"key":["할 수 있어요","가려고 해요","조금"]},{"instruction":"Abilities and plans.","items":["I can speak Korean","I can eat kimchi","I plan to go to Korea"],"key":["한국어를 할 수 있어요","김치를 먹을 수 있어요","한국에 가려고 해요"]},{"instruction":"Ask.","items":["Can you speak Korean?","What do you plan to do?"],"key":["한국어를 할 수 있어요","뭐 하려고 해요"]}]}}]},{"id":"B1-U2","title":"Family and age","lessons":[{"id":"B1-U2-L1","title":"Family and 님 honorifics","learn":"Family + respect! MY folks (humble): 아빠/엄마 fine at home. YOUR family (polite): 아버님, 어머님 (+님!). Elders get 세요 verbs: 드세요 (please eat, honorific)!","vocab":[{"t":"가족","r":"gajok","en":"family","pos":"noun"},{"t":"아버지","r":"abeoji","en":"father","pos":"noun"},{"t":"어머니","r":"eomeoni","en":"mother","pos":"noun"},{"t":"형제","r":"hyeongje","en":"brothers / siblings","pos":"noun"},{"t":"자매","r":"jamae","en":"sisters","pos":"noun"},{"t":"아들","r":"adeul","en":"son","pos":"noun"},{"t":"딸","r":"ttal","en":"daughter","pos":"noun"},{"t":"부모님","r":"bumonim","en":"parents (honorific)","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"+님 and 세요 honorifics","explain":"부모님 (honored parents), 선생님 (honored teacher). Verbs: 드세요 (honorific eat), 계세요 (honorific be). Elevate ELDERS, humble YOURSELF with 저!","pattern":"님-titles · 세요-verbs for elders","examples":[{"t":"아버지는 선생님이세요.","r":"abeoji-neun seonsaeng-nimiseyo.","en":"My father is a teacher. (honored)"},{"t":"어머님은?","r":"eomeonim-eun?","en":"And your mother? (honored)"},{"t":"가족이 네 명이에요.","r":"gajog-i ne myeong-ieyo.","en":"My family is four people."}],"mistakes":["Saying 엄마 to elders about YOUR mum — humble at home, polite outside!","Forgetting 님 for teachers: 선생님, not 선생!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"미나","t":"가족이 몇 명이에요?","r":"gajog-i myeot myeong-ieyo?","en":"How many in your family?"},{"sp":"지훈","t":"네 명이에요. 부모님과 저예요.","r":"ne myeong-ieyo. bumonim-gwa jeo-yeyo.","en":"Four. Parents and me (and one more)!"},{"sp":"미나","t":"형제가 있어요?","r":"hyeongje-ga iss-eoyo?","en":"Do you have brothers?"},{"sp":"지훈","t":"네, 형이 있어요!","r":"ne, hyeong-i iss-eoyo!","en":"Yes, I have an older brother! (m speaking)"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: My father is a teacher (honored)","answer":"아버지는 선생님이세요"},{"type":"fill","q":"___은? (Your honored mother?)","answer":"어머님"},{"type":"choose","q":"'How many in your family?' is…","options":["가족이 뭐예요","가족이 몇 명이에요","가족이 어디예요","가족이 누구예요"],"answer":"가족이 몇 명이에요"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: 선생님이세요 / 아버지는","answer":"아버지는 선생님이세요"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: 아버지는 선생님이세요.","answer":"아버지는 선생님이세요."}],"quiz":[{"q":"님 adds…","options":["plural","honor","past","question"],"answer":1,"why":"부모님 = honored parents."},{"q":"선생님 means…","options":["teacher","honored teacher","student","parent"],"answer":1,"why":"님 is required for teachers!"},{"q":"부모님 means…","options":["brothers","honored parents","children","family"],"answer":1,"why":"부모 + 님."},{"q":"딸 means…","options":["son","daughter","sister","mother"],"answer":1,"why":"딸 = daughter."},{"q":"네 명 means…","options":["4 things","4 people","4th","four times"],"answer":1,"why":"명 counts people."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Family worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Korean.","items":["family","father","daughter"],"key":["가족","아버지","딸"]},{"instruction":"Honor family.","items":["My father is a teacher (honored)","And your mother? (honored)"],"key":["아버지는 선생님이세요","어머님은"]},{"instruction":"Count family.","items":["How many in your family?","Four people"],"key":["가족이 몇 명이에요","네 명이에요"]}]}},{"id":"B1-U2-L2","title":"Age: 몇 살","learn":"Age: 몇 살이에요? (How old?) → 스무 살이에요 (I'm 20). 살 counts years with NATIVE numbers! Birthdays: 생일이 언제예요? → 삼월이에요! Months: 월, days: 일!","vocab":[{"t":"몇 살","r":"myeot sal","en":"how old","pos":"phrase"},{"t":"스무 살","r":"seumu sal","en":"20 years old","pos":"noun"},{"t":"생일","r":"saeng-il","en":"birthday","pos":"noun"},{"t":"언제","r":"eonje","en":"when","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"매년","r":"maenyeon","en":"every year","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"축하","r":"chukha","en":"congratulations","pos":"noun"},{"t":"선물","r":"seonmul","en":"present","pos":"noun"},{"t":"케이크","r":"keikeu","en":"cake","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"살 (native age) · 월/일 dates","explain":"스무 살 (20), 열일곱 살 (17). Months SINO: 일월 (Jan), 삼월 (Mar). Days: 삼일 (3rd), 이십일 (21st)!","pattern":"native + 살 · sino + 월/일","examples":[{"t":"스무 살이에요.","r":"seumu sal-ieyo.","en":"I'm twenty."},{"t":"생일은 삼월이에요.","r":"saeng-il-eun samwol-ieyo.","en":"My birthday is March."},{"t":"생일 축하해요!","r":"saeng-il chukhahaeyo!","en":"Happy birthday!"}],"mistakes":["Saying 이십 살 — 20 is 스무 살!","Saying 삼달 — months are 월!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"지훈","t":"몇 살이에요?","r":"myeot sal-ieyo?","en":"How old are you?"},{"sp":"미나","t":"스무 살이에요!","r":"seumu sal-ieyo!","en":"I'm twenty!"},{"sp":"지훈","t":"생일이 언제예요?","r":"saeng-il-i eonjeyeyo?","en":"When is your birthday?"},{"sp":"미나","t":"삼월이에요!","r":"samwol-ieyo!","en":"It's March!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I'm twenty","answer":"스무 살이에요"},{"type":"fill","q":"생일은 ___이에요. (March)","answer":"삼월"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Happy birthday!' is…","options":["새해 복 많이","생일 축하해요","축하합니다 새해","수고했어요"],"answer":"생일 축하해요"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: 이에요 / 몇 살","answer":"몇 살이에요"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: 스무 살이에요.","answer":"스무 살이에요."}],"quiz":[{"q":"스무 살 means…","options":["12","20","22","10"],"answer":1,"why":"스무 살 = 20 years."},{"q":"삼월 means…","options":["March","3 days","3 years","May"],"answer":0,"why":"삼 + 월 = March."},{"q":"생일 means…","options":["age","birthday","year","party"],"answer":1,"why":"생일 = birthday."},{"q":"언제 means…","options":["where","when","who","how"],"answer":1,"why":"언제 = when."},{"q":"매년 means…","options":["every day","every year","last year","next year"],"answer":1,"why":"매년 = every year."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Age worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Korean.","items":["how old","birthday","present"],"key":["몇 살","생일","선물"]},{"instruction":"Ages and dates.","items":["I'm twenty","My birthday is March","Happy birthday!"],"key":["스무 살이에요","생일은 삼월이에요","생일 축하해요"]},{"instruction":"Ask.","items":["How old are you?","When is your birthday?"],"key":["몇 살이에요","생일이 언제예요"]}]}}]},{"id":"B1-U3","title":"Opinions and weather","lessons":[{"id":"B1-U3-L1","title":"Opinions: -고 생각해요","learn":"Think out loud! -고 생각해요 (I think that…): 지하철이 좋다고 생각해요! Compare: 더 (more), 제일 (most): 이게 제일 좋아요 = This is the best! 보다 = than!","vocab":[{"t":"생각해요","r":"saenggakhaeyo","en":"to think","pos":"verb"},{"t":"믿어요","r":"mid-eoyo","en":"to believe","pos":"verb"},{"t":"좋아요","r":"jo-ayo","en":"good","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"나빠요","r":"nappayo","en":"bad","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"더","r":"deo","en":"more","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"제일","r":"je-il","en":"most / best","pos":"adverb"},{"t":"의견","r":"uigyeon","en":"opinion","pos":"noun"},{"t":"찬성","r":"chanseong","en":"agreement","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"-고 생각해요 + 더/제일 + 보다","explain":"지하철이 좋다고 생각해요 (I think the subway is good). 더 커요 (bigger), 제일 좋아요 (best). 차보다 커요 = bigger THAN the car!","pattern":"quote-고 생각해요 · 보다 + 더","examples":[{"t":"지하철이 좋다고 생각해요.","r":"jihacheol-i jotago saenggakhaeyo.","en":"I think the subway is good."},{"t":"이게 더 커요.","r":"ige deo keoyo.","en":"This is bigger."},{"t":"이게 제일 좋아요!","r":"ige je-il jo-ayo!","en":"This is the best!"}],"mistakes":["Saying 좋아요고 생각해요 — quote: 좋다고 생각해요!","Forgetting 보다: than = 보다!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"미나","t":"지하철이 좋다고 생각해요.","r":"jihacheol-i jotago saenggakhaeyo.","en":"I think the subway is good."},{"sp":"지훈","t":"저는 차가 빠르다고 생각해요.","r":"jeo-neun cha-ga ppareudago saenggakhaeyo.","en":"I think the car is fast."},{"sp":"미나","t":"하지만 지하철이 더 싸요!","r":"hajiman jihacheol-i deo ssayo!","en":"But the subway is cheaper!"},{"sp":"지훈","t":"찬성이에요!","r":"chanseong-ieyo!","en":"I agree!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I think the subway is good","answer":"지하철이 좋다고 생각해요"},{"type":"fill","q":"이게 ___ 좋아요! (most)","answer":"제일"},{"type":"choose","q":"'This is bigger' is…","options":["이게 커요","이게 더 커요","이게 제일 커요","이게 크다고 생각해요"],"answer":"이게 더 커요"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: 생각해요 / 좋다고 / 지하철이","answer":"지하철이 좋다고 생각해요"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: 지하철이 좋다고 생각해요.","answer":"지하철이 좋다고 생각해요."}],"quiz":[{"q":"-고 생각해요 attaches to…","options":["요-form","quote-form (다고)","past only","commands"],"answer":1,"why":"좋다고 생각해요 — quote + 고."},{"q":"더 means…","options":["most","more","best","less"],"answer":1,"why":"더 = more."},{"q":"제일 means…","options":["more","most","first time","number one only"],"answer":1,"why":"제일 = most/best."},{"q":"나빠요 means…","options":["good","bad","big","small"],"answer":1,"why":"나빠요 = bad."},{"q":"찬성이에요 means…","options":["I disagree","I agree","maybe","never"],"answer":1,"why":"찬성 = agreement."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Opinions worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Korean.","items":["to think","more","opinion"],"key":["생각해요","더","의견"]},{"instruction":"Think and compare.","items":["I think the subway is good","This is bigger","This is the best"],"key":["지하철이 좋다고 생각해요","이게 더 커요","이게 제일 좋아요"]},{"instruction":"Debate.","items":["But the subway is cheaper!","I agree!"],"key":["하지만 지하철이 더 싸요","찬성이에요"]}]}},{"id":"B1-U3-L2","title":"Weather: 날씨","learn":"Weather talk! 날씨가 어때요? (How's the weather?) → 추워요 (It's cold). 비가 와요 (It rains), 눈이 와요 (It snows). Adjective past: 추웠어요 (was cold)!","vocab":[{"t":"날씨","r":"nalssi","en":"weather","pos":"noun"},{"t":"태양","r":"taeyang","en":"sun","pos":"noun"},{"t":"비","r":"bi","en":"rain","pos":"noun"},{"t":"눈","r":"nun","en":"snow","pos":"noun"},{"t":"추워요","r":"chuweoyo","en":"cold","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"더워요","r":"deoweoyo","en":"hot","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"따뜻해요","r":"ttatteutaeyo","en":"warm","pos":"adjective"},{"t":"바람","r":"baram","en":"wind","pos":"noun"}],"grammar":{"title":"비가 와요 · 추웠어요","explain":"비가 와요 (rain comes = it rains), 눈이 와요 (it snows). Past: 추웠어요 (was cold), 더웠어요 (was hot). 내일은 따뜻해요 (tomorrow is warm)!","pattern":"비/눈 + 가/이 와요 · adjective + 었어요","examples":[{"t":"오늘은 추워요.","r":"oneul-eun chuweoyo.","en":"Today is cold."},{"t":"비가 와요.","r":"bi-ga wayo.","en":"It rains."},{"t":"어제는 추웠어요.","r":"eoje-neun chuwoss-eoyo.","en":"Yesterday was cold."}],"mistakes":["Saying 비를 와요 — rain needs 가!","Saying 춥었어요 — 춥다 contracts: 추웠어요!"]},"dialogue":[{"sp":"지훈","t":"날씨가 어때요?","r":"nalssi-ga eottaeyo?","en":"How is the weather?"},{"sp":"미나","t":"추워요! 눈이 와요!","r":"chuweoyo! nun-i wayo!","en":"It's cold! It's snowing!"},{"sp":"지훈","t":"내일은 따뜻해요?","r":"nae-il-eun ttatteutaeyo?","en":"Will it be warm tomorrow?"},{"sp":"미나","t":"네! 산책해요!","r":"ne! sanchaekhaeyo!","en":"Yes! Let's take a walk!"}],"practice":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: It rains","answer":"비가 와요"},{"type":"fill","q":"오늘은 ___. (cold)","answer":"추워요"},{"type":"choose","q":"'How is the weather?' is…","options":["날씨가 뭐예요","날씨가 어때요","날씨가 어디예요","날씨가 언제예요"],"answer":"날씨가 어때요"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: 와요 / 비가","answer":"비가 와요"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: 추워요! 눈이 와요!","answer":"추워요! 눈이 와요!"}],"quiz":[{"q":"비가 와요 means…","options":["it snows","it rains","it's windy","it's sunny"],"answer":1,"why":"와요 = comes."},{"q":"추웠어요 means…","options":["is cold","was cold","not cold","will cold"],"answer":1,"why":"었어요 = past."},{"q":"내일은 따뜻해요 means…","options":["today warm","tomorrow warm","yesterday warm","always warm"],"answer":1,"why":"내일 = tomorrow."},{"q":"Adjective past adds…","options":["겠어요","었/았어요","고 싶어요","려고 해요"],"answer":1,"why":"추워→추웠어요."},{"q":"눈 means…","options":["rain","snow","wind","sun"],"answer":1,"why":"눈 = snow (also eye!)."}],"flashcards":"auto:vocab","worksheet":{"title":"Weather worksheet","tasks":[{"instruction":"Translate to Korean.","items":["weather","snow","cold"],"key":["날씨","눈","추워요"]},{"instruction":"Report weather.","items":["It rains","Today is cold","Yesterday was cold"],"key":["비가 와요","오늘은 추워요","어제는 추웠어요"]},{"instruction":"Ask and plan.","items":["How is the weather?","Let's take a walk!"],"key":["날씨가 어때요","산책해요"]}]}}]}],"test":{"title":"B1 final test","items":[{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say (formal): Today I don't eat","answer":"오늘은 먹지 않아요"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I can speak Korean","answer":"한국어를 할 수 있어요"},{"type":"choose","q":"'My father is a teacher (honored)'","options":["아빠는 선생님이야","아버지는 선생님이세요","아버지는 선생님이에요","선생님은 아버지세요"],"answer":"아버지는 선생님이세요"},{"type":"translate_t","q":"추워요! 눈이 와요!","answer":"It's cold! It's snowing!"},{"type":"fill","q":"한국에 가___ 해요. (plan to)","answer":"려고"},{"type":"choose","q":"'Because I'm sick. So I rest'","options":["아파서 쉬어요","왜냐하면 아파요. 그래서 쉬어요","아프니까 쉴 거예요","아파도 쉬어요"],"answer":"왜냐하면 아파요. 그래서 쉬어요"},{"type":"reorder","q":"Order: 와요 / 비가","answer":"비가 와요"},{"type":"speak","q":"Say aloud: 지하철이 좋다고 생각해요.","answer":"지하철이 좋다고 생각해요."},{"type":"fill","q":"이게 ___ 좋아요! (most)","answer":"제일"},{"type":"translate_en","q":"Say: I think the subway is good","answer":"지하철이 좋다고 생각해요"}]}}}